# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD starts rsyncd (detached) with the vulnerable open module,
# then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the daemon is ALREADY RUNNING (open, unauthenticated) when the agent
#     starts, so a dead daemon is a genuine FAIL;
#   * PID 1's main child is `sleep infinity`, so restarting rsyncd cannot kill
#     the container.
#
# Note on "not restarted": rsyncd re-reads /etc/rsyncd.conf on EVERY incoming
# connection, so a config fix takes effect without any restart. There is
# therefore no "fixed the config but forgot to restart" failure case for this
# scenario.
